+
+## Stop-Hook Completion Fallback (2026-08)
+
+When a tmux phase's Stop hook never writes `.done`, the wait used to drain to
+its full deadline and land a terminal error (`claude stop hook did not signal
+completion`) even when the agent had demonstrably finished — artifacts on
+disk, fix commits in the worktree. Since this change, the tmux wait paths can
+consult a shared completion predicate
+(`Hive::ClaudeCompletionEvaluator`, see
+`docs/notes/review-stop-hook-completion-fallback.md`): when the caller's
+evidence proves clean completion, Hive emits a WARN-level
+`claude_completion_fallback` event in `events.jsonl` and lets the stage
+succeed. Crashes, usage walls, unreadable/gone tmux sessions, exit != 0, and
+missing required artifacts still fail exactly as before.
+
+Mode guidance: `claude.mode: headless` remains the recommended setting for
+hive versions without this fix; tmux mode is safe once it is deployed. Hive
+never auto-reverts an operator's configured mode.
+
diff --git a/docs/notes/review-stop-hook-completion-fallback.md b/docs/notes/review-stop-hook-completion-fallback.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..ddb0ce8a6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/notes/review-stop-hook-completion-fallback.md
@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@
+# Tmux Claude Stop-Hook Completion Fallback
+
+**Date:** 2026-08-25
+**Scope:** `lib/hive/claude_launcher.rb`, `lib/hive/claude_completion_evaluator.rb`, `lib/hive/stop_hook_installer.rb`, `lib/hive/scripts/stop_hook.sh`, the 6-review wrappers (`review.rb`, `review/ci_fix.rb`, `review/triage.rb`, `review/browser_test.rb`)
+
+## Incident
+
+Claude-backed review-fix passes in tmux mode completed real work (artifacts
+written, commits made, `agent_end phase=fix pass=01 phase complete` events,
+sometimes even a later `clean_exit_auto_committed`) yet Hive wrote a terminal
+`REVIEW_ERROR phase=fix reason=fix_failed pass=N message="claude stop hook did not signal completion"`.
+Tasks 58 (PR #622), 287 (PR #623), and 288 (PR #624) were stranded this way on
+2026-06-29.
+
+## Signal chain
+
+1. `StopHookInstaller.install` writes `.claude/settings.json` into the task
+   folder AND the launch cwd, each pointing at `scripts/stop_hook.sh` with
+   `HIVE_TASK_STAGE_DIR=<stage dir>`.
+2. When Claude Code fires its Stop hook, `stop_hook.sh` writes
+   `<stage_dir>/result.json` and touches `<stage_dir>/.done`.
+3. `ClaudeLauncher.wait_for_done_signal` (exit_code_only mode — used by the
+   review fix agent and CI-fix agent) polls `<task.folder>/.done` until
+   `timeout_sec` (default 2700s for review fix), then returns
+   `{status: :timeout, error_message: "claude stop hook did not signal completion"}`.
+4. `Review.agent_failed?` classifies `:timeout` as failure → terminal
+   REVIEW_ERROR.
+
+## Hypotheses investigated
+
+| # | Hypothesis | Verdict |
+|---|------------|---------|
+| H1 | Sentinel path mismatch between installer / hook script / launcher | **Refuted.** All three now derive from one source: `StopHookInstaller::DONE_FILENAME` / `RESULT_FILENAME` constants, pinned by round-trip tests (`test/unit/stop_hook_installer_test.rb`). The launcher's `done_path` / `result_path` delegate to them. |
+| H2 | Poll timeout shorter than real fix-pass runtime | **Refuted.** `wait_for_done_signal` uses the caller-supplied `timeout_sec` (review fix default 2700s); no shorter internal ceiling exists. |
+| H3 | Hook script fails silently so the sentinel is never written (missing `/bin/sh` env, unwritable stage dir, Claude Code passing no stdin, hook disabled by settings resolution drift between cwd and `--add-dir`) | **Unproven but plausible.** The hook runs under `set -eu`; any failure is swallowed by Claude Code and leaves no trace except an absent `.done`. The empty-stdin sentinel JSON in `stop_hook.sh` already distinguishes "hook ran, no payload". A silent hook failure is indistinguishable from "hook never fired" from Hive's side. |
+| H4 | Cleanup deleting the sentinel before it is read | **Refuted.** `reset_signal_files` runs only at spawn start; `cleanup_done` runs after the wait returns. No mid-wait deletion exists. |
+| H5 | tmux pane race: output/marker check runs before the hook flushes | **Refuted for exit_code_only**: that wait never inspects pane output for markers; it only polls `.done`. |
+| H6 | Claude Code version drift where the Stop hook does not fire on some clean exits (hook config not reloaded, hook silently skipped) | **Unproven — most likely root cause.** The evidence pattern (real work + commits + clean process exit + zero sentinel) is exactly what a silently-not-fired Stop hook produces. Not deterministically reproducible in CI; per plan Q7 we ship the tolerant fallback plus this documented hypothesis instead of a speculative hook-side fix. |
+
+## Mitigation shipped
+
+A shared completion fallback in the tmux control plane:
+
+- `Hive::ClaudeCompletionEvaluator` evaluates a strict predicate (ALL of:
+  missing-sentinel timeout only, no crash, session readable, worktree
+  readable, required artifacts exist and parse, commit-or-no-change-evidence
+  rule, no unresolved escalation, no missing-output marker).
+- `ClaudeLauncher.wait_for_done_signal` / `wait_for_expected_output` consult
+  an optional caller-supplied `completion_check:` closure at their deadline.
+  On a positive decision they emit a WARN-level `claude_completion_fallback`
+  audit event (payload: phase, pass, session, expected sentinel path,
+  missing-signal reason, artifacts checked, commit/no-change evidence, task
+  slug) and return `:ok` so the stage proceeds to SUCCESS.
+- Every strict failure mode keeps its exact previous behavior: crashes,
+  usage walls, unreadable/gone tmux, exit != 0, and missing required
+  artifacts still produce the same terminal markers.
+
+## Follow-up notes
+
+- Confirming/refuting H6 needs a Claude Code build where Stop-hook firing can
+  be observed directly (e.g., instrumenting `stop_hook.sh` with a timestamped
+  append-only log file). If it reproduces, prefer fixing the firing side over
+  widening the fallback predicate.
+- The fallback intentionally requires a new commit since pass start whenever
+  the pass claims code changes. Fix agents that leave uncommitted worktrees
+  still fail strictly; the orchestrator's scope-checked auto-commit cannot be
+  reached because evaluation happens before it would run.
+
+## Recovery of the stranded tasks
+
+After deploying this fix:
+
+1. Preferred (auditable): clear the marker with a reason and let the runner
+   re-evaluate through the new predicate:
+   ```sh
+   hive markers clear <task-folder> --name REVIEW_ERROR \
+     --reason "stop-hook completion fallback deployed; artifacts+commits verified"
+   hive run <task-folder>
+   ```
+2. Verify before clearing: pass artifacts under `reviews/` parse, the
+   worktree contains the fix commits, and `events.jsonl` shows
+   `agent_end phase=fix ... phase complete`. Never clear without that trail.
+
+Operator mode guidance: `claude.mode: headless` remains the recommended
+setting for versions without this fix; tmux mode is safe once this change is
+deployed. Do not auto-revert operator config.
diff --git a/lib/hive/claude_completion_evaluator.rb b/lib/hive/claude_completion_evaluator.rb
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..1b9e92243
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/hive/claude_completion_evaluator.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,105 @@
+module Hive
+  module ClaudeCompletionEvaluator
+    Decision = Data.define(:fallback_ok?, :failed_condition, :evidence)
+
+    CONDITION_ORDER = %i[
+      sentinel_missing
+      exit_timeout_only
+      not_crashed
+      session_readable
+      worktree_readable
+      artifacts_exist_and_parse
+      commit_or_no_change_evidence
+      no_unresolved_escalation
+      no_missing_output_marker
+    ].freeze
+
+    module_function
+
+    def evaluate(context)
+      evidence = normalize(context)
+      failed = CONDITION_ORDER.find { |condition| !send(condition, evidence) }
+      Decision.new(
+        fallback_ok?: failed.nil?,
+        failed_condition: failed,
+        evidence: evidence
+      )
+    end
+
+    def normalize(context)
+      context = context.to_h
+      {
+        sentinel_seen: bool(context[:sentinel_seen]),
+        exit_status: context[:exit_status],
+        crashed: bool(context[:crashed]),
+        session_readable: bool(context[:session_readable]),
+        worktree_readable: bool(context.fetch(:worktree_readable, true)),
+        required_artifacts: Array(context[:required_artifacts]),
+        change_claimed: bool(context.fetch(:change_claimed, true)),
+        new_commit_since_start: bool(context[:new_commit_since_start]),
+        no_change_evidence: bool(context[:no_change_evidence]),
+        unresolved_escalation: bool(context[:unresolved_escalation]),
+        missing_output_marker: bool(context[:missing_output_marker])
+      }
+    end
+
+    def sentinel_missing(evidence)
+      !evidence[:sentinel_seen]
+    end
+
+    def exit_timeout_only(evidence)
+      evidence[:exit_status] == :timeout
+    end
+
+    def not_crashed(evidence)
+      !evidence[:crashed]
+    end
+
+    def session_readable(evidence)
+      evidence[:session_readable]
+    end
+
+    def worktree_readable(evidence)
+      evidence[:worktree_readable]
+    end
+
+    def artifacts_exist_and_parse(evidence)
+      evidence[:required_artifacts].all? { |artifact| artifact_parses?(artifact) }
+    end
+
+    def artifact_parses?(artifact)
+      path = artifact[:path].to_s
+      return false if path.empty?
+      return false unless File.exist?(path)
+      return false unless File.size(path).positive?
+
+      parser = artifact[:parser]
+      return true unless parser
+
+      body = File.read(path)
+      !!parser.call(body)
+    rescue StandardError
+      false
+    end
+
+    def commit_or_no_change_evidence(evidence)
+      if evidence[:change_claimed]
+        evidence[:new_commit_since_start]
+      else
+        evidence[:new_commit_since_start] || evidence[:no_change_evidence]
+      end
+    end
+
+    def no_unresolved_escalation(evidence)
+      !evidence[:unresolved_escalation]
+    end
+
+    def no_missing_output_marker(evidence)
+      !evidence[:missing_output_marker]
+    end
+
+    def bool(value)
+      value == true
+    end
+  end
+end
