+timestamp: 2026-08-25T00:00:00Z
+title: Tmux Claude stop-hook completion fallback unstrands clean fix passes
+---
+
+- Tmux-launched phases (review fix, CI-fix, triage, browser-test) can now recover from the missing `.done` sentinel incident: `ClaudeLauncher` wait paths consult `Hive::ClaudeCompletionEvaluator` via a caller-supplied `completion_check:` closure and, on a strict all-conditions pass (exit-timeout only, readable session/worktree, required artifacts parse, commit-or-no-change evidence, no unresolved escalation), emit a WARN-level `claude_completion_fallback` event and return `:ok`.
+- Strict failure modes are unchanged: crashes, usage walls, unreadable/gone tmux, exit != 0, and missing artifacts still produce terminal errors with the same messages.
+- Sentinel filenames are now single-sourced in `StopHookInstaller::DONE_FILENAME` / `RESULT_FILENAME` with installer→hook→launcher round-trip contract tests.
